<title>GERMANY: Fresenius starts new dialysis unit group.</title>
<headline>Fresenius starts new dialysis unit group.</headline>
<dateline>BAD HOMBURG, Germany 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>German medical technology group Fresenius AG said on Friday it was putting its German dialysis activities into a new wholly-owned unit to be called Fresenius Medical Care Deutschland GmbH.</p>
<p>Fresenius said the move was part of plans to acquire National Medical Care Inc from U.S.-based W.R. Grace. The subsidiary, slated to begin operations on September 1, will have about 1,860 employees.</p>
<p>Fresenius said the deal with Grace faces a vote by Grace shareholders on September 16. If the deal is approved, Fresenius said the acquisition would be completed in September.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
